  "worked_solution": "We can solve this equation by taking the $7$th root of each side and solving for $x.$\nSince $n=7$ is odd, there is only one real solution to this equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)^{7} & =-128 \\\\ \\sqrt[7]{(x-3)^{7}} & =\\sqrt[7]{-128} \\\\ x-3 & =\\sqrt[7]{(-2)^{7}} \\\\ x-3 & =-2 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=1.$",
